<!--
    kuna issue testcase: an AIF gap candidate that is a fragment of the known
    function around it is not a function (`option aifbracket on|off`,
    default-ON).

    Issue:      kuna GH-299 - aif plants mid-function entries on a large i386
                PE, a third of them inside a function kuna already knows.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the AIF gap-walk accept
                (`analyzers/aif/kuna_aifbracket.rs`).
    P0 assert:  `option aifbracket on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  Every pass clears
    it and loads `aifbracket_pe_i386.exe` (source `aifbracket_pe_i386.asm`
    beside it): 22 leaf functions with one prologue, `dispatch` at 0x4011f0
    whose block at 0x4011fd is reached only through `jmp dword [ebp+12]` and
    jumps back to `dispatch`'s tail, and `shared` at 0x401210, a real function
    behind a pointer after int3 padding that jumps to the same tail.

    Pass 1 (`mode aggressive`, `option aifbracket off`) reproduces the bug:
    the inventory lists sub_4011fd inside `dispatch`.
    Pass 2 (`mode aggressive`, shipped default) drops it and keeps sub_401210.
    Pass 3 (`mode aggressive`, `option aif off`) shows sub_401210 is the gap
    walk's own find, so pass 2 kept an AIF accept rather than missing one.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
